## Business interpretation
The index can help retailers and analysts monitor the direction of real retail sales volumes and plan broad inventory, staffing, and promotional scenarios. It is a sector-level indicator: it cannot identify individual companies, products, or store-level demand.

Forecasts should be treated as planning estimates, not certain outcomes. Unexpected economic conditions, price changes, consumer confidence, and revisions to ONS data may affect actual results.

## Limitations
- The series is a national retail-sector index, not company- or product-level sales.
- Only one selected ONS series was modelled.
- The evaluation period contains 12 months; performance may differ in other periods.
- The forecast is a statistical extrapolation and does not include explanatory variables such as inflation, wages, or consumer confidence.

